1. The Regency Government in the effort to protect Children shall and is responsible for:
a. respecting the fulfillment of Children's rights without distinguishing ethnicity, religion, race, class, gender, ethnicity, culture and language, legal status, birth order, and physical and/or mental condition;
b. providing support for facilities, infrastructure, and availability of human resources in the implementation of Child Protection;
c. guaranteeing the protection, care, and welfare of Children by taking into account the rights and obligations of Parents, Guardians, or other persons legally responsible for the Child;
d. guaranteeing Children to convey their right to express opinions in accordance with the age and level of intelligence of the Child;
e. establishing and implementing policies and programs/activities for the protection of Children's rights;
f. cooperating with the community and/or Community Organizations in the implementation of Child Protection in accordance with the provisions of Laws and Regulations;
g. conducting rehabilitation for Children who are victims of violence;
h. providing special protection to Children:
1\. in emergency situations victims of disasters and conflicts;
2\. in conflict with the law;
3\. victims of violence, neglect and trafficking in persons;
4\. from minority and isolated groups;
5\. who are exploited economically and/or sexually/victims of pornography;
6\. who are victims of narcotics, alcohol, psychotropic abuse; and
7\. identified with HIV/AIDS;
i. organizing inclusive education for Children with special needs;
j. taking preventive action in order to prevent violations against Children; and
k. implementing and supporting National policies in the implementation of Child Protection in the Regency carried out through efforts to realize Child-Friendly Regency, Child-Friendly Sub-district and Child-Friendly Village;
2. The responsibility of the Regency Government in the effort to protect Children as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented by DPPPA.

